      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree some protection is nice-to-have, but visible medical icon is totally bad idea IMHO because:\n\n1. really bad guys can hurt / discriminate those people more easily.\n2. this creates pressure for every user to understand every medical icons, and there's no limit to the number of medical conditions that should be supported.\n\n1 is easier point to see, but 2 is more problematic in longer term IMO, because it will turn the VRChat society into \"pretend-to-be-good-citizen\" game, much more akin to real politics. (imagine the tutorial contains 2-hour long mandatory lessons on real-world medical conditions, blah blah)\n\nI think client-side option for making rendering low-constrast or de-colored (w/o any visible icon / badges) is much better.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
